    <widget_type>Label</widget_type>
    <enabled>true</enabled>
    <text>start SNL = start stand-alone SNL program that holds the whole EMU process

upper = detection of the upper edge of the beam
lower = detection of the lower edge  of the beam
wide scan = detection of Vpeak and deltaV at one precise position

Vpeak = V for Ibeam maximum
deltaV = beam width in Volt
upper-lower = beam width in mm

Vstart  = Vpeak + deltaV/2.
Vend  = Vpeak  - deltaV/2.
Vstep = ( Vstart - Vend ) / (HV points*2)
              - value for each power supply -
V1 = emups1 :  from (+Vstart / 2) to  (+Vend / 2)
V2 = emups2 :  from (-Vstart  / 2) to  (-Vend / 2)

Example :
V1         : progression from start =  +5000 V  to end =  -5000 V
V2         : progression from start =  -5000 V   to end = +5000V
(V1-V2) : progression from start = +10000V to end  = -10000V

Beam acquisition during process (see FACQ panel) :
- emittance measurement only works with an external trigger.
- the external trigger is provided by the Timing System (TREP).
- end of acquisition must be less or equal than TREP.
- only one acquisition can be defined in a display.

Motor motions controls through the MaxV VME card :
 - to use it for the EMU process
    1) servo / maxv "Enable" to obtain green leds on maxv and servo
    2) use "MoveAbs" or "tweak" for simple motions
 - when measurement is over
    1) "MoveAbs" =0   *** never use "home" cmd on expert panel ***
    2)  servo / maxv "Disable" to obtain red leds on maxv and servo

(if you have lost the control of the mechanism after having reach a 
 switch limit on the servostar system (LET8), see Help on  motor panel)</text>
    <font>
      <fontdata fontName="Arial" height="10" style="0" />
